# AWS CCP — Networking & Content Delivery

Which service gives you a logically isolated private network inside AWS?
---
VPC
= Amazon VPC
= Virtual Private Cloud
---
Your own address range, subnets, route tables, and gateways.

What makes a subnet public?
---
A route to an internet gateway
~ Being in a specific Availability Zone
~ A security group rule
~ Having more than one instance
---
Public and private are properties of the route table, not the subnet itself.

Which VPC component lets instances in private subnets reach out to the internet without being reachable from it?
---
NAT gateway
= NAT
= a NAT gateway
---
Outbound only, for updates and API calls. Inbound still requires a public-facing path.

Which component connects a VPC to the internet?
---
internet gateway
= IGW
= an internet gateway
---
Attached to the VPC, referenced by public subnets' route tables.

Which service is AWS's DNS, translating domain names to IP addresses with health checks and routing policies?
---
Route 53
= Amazon Route 53
= Route53
---
The name is a pun on DNS port 53. Routing policies include latency, weighted, and failover.

Which service caches your content at edge locations so users get it with low latency?
---
CloudFront
= Amazon CloudFront
---
The AWS CDN. Also the front line where Shield and WAF absorb attacks.

Which option provides a dedicated, private physical connection from your data center to AWS?
---
Direct Connect
~ Site-to-Site VPN
~ Internet gateway
~ Global Accelerator
---
Consistent bandwidth, weeks to provision. The VPN is the quick alternative.

Which option encrypts traffic between your network and AWS over the public internet?
---
Site-to-Site VPN
~ Direct Connect
~ VPC peering
~ CloudFront
---
Up in hours, but throughput and latency ride on internet conditions.

Which service lets you create, publish, and throttle APIs for your backends?
---
API Gateway
= Amazon API Gateway
---
REST and WebSocket APIs with auth, throttling, and caching. A natural front door for Lambda.

Which service routes users onto the AWS global network at the nearest edge, using two static anycast IPs?
---
Global Accelerator
~ CloudFront
~ Route 53
~ Direct Connect
---
CloudFront caches content. Global Accelerator accelerates dynamic traffic all the way to your origin.

Which feature connects two VPCs so they route traffic to each other privately?
---
VPC peering
~ An internet gateway
~ A NAT gateway
~ CloudFront
---
Peering is one-to-one and not transitive. Transit Gateway is the hub for many VPCs.

VPC {{Flow Logs}} capture information about the IP traffic going to and from network interfaces.
---
The raw material for network troubleshooting, and one of GuardDuty's inputs.
